The Spanish word list in src/translations/onyx-translations-es.js is derived from the Spanish wordnet of the
Multilingual Central Repository 3.0 (http://adimen.si.ehu.es/web/MCR/), as distributed in the Open Multilingual
Wordnet 1.4 (https://omwn.org/), under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported license (CC BY 3.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). Onyx changed it: it chose, for each English word, the Spanish words
most common in Spanish (ranked with wordfreq), and the most common English words for each Spanish word.

A. Gonzalez-Agirre, E. Laparra and G. Rigau. Multilingual Central Repository version 3.0: upgrading a very large
lexical knowledge base. Proceedings of the 6th Global WordNet Conference (GWC 2012), Matsue.

